    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d94-a1-a3">

                <pb facs="0262" n="204" sameAs="frus:frus1866p3/pg204"/>


                <head ana="#head_untitled-missing-head-in-printed-volume">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Colonization Office, No.</hi> 13 <hi
                                rendition="#italic">S. Juan de Letran,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-12-06"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >December</hi> 6, 1865.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>S<hi rendition="#small-caps">ir:</hi> Your letter by Mr. Arroyo was received too
                    late to reply by the steamer of to-day.</p>
                <p>Your suggestion as to a bureau of correspondence in New York is good, and seems
                    to be well worthy of his majesty’s consideration.</p>
                <p>There is in the United States a lamentable state of ignorance concerning Mexico
                    and the Mexicans, and any one who can dispel that ignorance may well be
                    considered as having done a good work.</p>
                <p>I enclose some decrees and other documents which you may find interesting.</p>
                <p>Respectfully, and your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>M. F. MAURY, <hi rendition="#italic">Imperial
                        Commissioner.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>E. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Farrenne</hi>. <hi rendition="#italic">New
                            York.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
